From: POLARIS Phase 4b benchmark trace patch
Subject: Add KV cache allocation tracing for vLLM

This patch adds POLARIS trace collection to vLLM's KVCacheManager.
Set environment variable POLARIS_TRACE=<output_path> before launching
vLLM, and every KV cache block allocation/free event will be written
to the specified CSV file.

The trace format (compatible with polaris-workload trace-replay):
    timestamp_ns,op,session_id,token_start,token_count

Ops emitted:
  - SESSION_CREATE: first allocation for a request
  - BLOCK_ALLOC: each block allocated (with token range)
  - BLOCK_FREE: each block freed
  - SESSION_DESTROY: request freed from KV cache

Intended vLLM version: commit 132765e3560659ff63ebd236203672e991b70e08
Applies to: vllm/v1/core/kv_cache_manager.py

Usage:
  POLARIS_TRACE=/tmp/vllm_trace.csv vllm serve <model>
  # After benchmark completes, copy /tmp/vllm_trace.csv to your
  # POLARIS benchmarks/traces/ directory for replay.

How to apply:
  patch -p1 < benchmarks/patches/vllm/trace_kv_cache.patch
  # (run this command from the vLLM repository root)

How to revert:
  patch -R -p1 < benchmarks/patches/vllm/trace_kv_cache.patch

Note: This is purely additive. Zero changes to vLLM's behavior.

